#{[17592186659668 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt[3]{{x}^{2}}},\\, & 1<x<8 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=\\sqrt[3]{X},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] [17592186659672 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x+1}{4},\\, & 0<x<2 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=4X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] [17592186659675 "![](images/48/483c019e9c68f857379192d2b40ab84803c4360ca4e0158adc0a8a3bc1636c4e.png)\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}xy, & (x,y)\\in D, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $F(x,y)$ is the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y,$ find $F(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{5}{2}).$"] [17592186659678 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x}{9{y}^{2}}, & 1\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le 4, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x>2,\\,y>4.$"] [17592186659700 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3\\sqrt{x}}{2},\\, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=\\sqrt{X},$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] [17592186659710 "![](images/3c/3c45364ee569d9ee24bbac167ad2a76f8a0a1a519f6604b7f9427d723c59abab.png)\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6y{e}^{-3x}, & (x,y)\\in D, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $F(x,y)$ is the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y,$ find $F(1,-\\frac{1}{3}).$"] [17592186659715 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{{x}^{2}},\\, & 1<x<2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=2X+1,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] [17592186659740 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{e}^{1-x},\\, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=-\\frac{1}{2}X,$ then what is the probability density function of $Y?$"] [17592186659741 "Let $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{5}y\\sqrt{x}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 4 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nFind the expression for the corresponding joint CDF when $x>1$ and $1\\le y\\le 4.$"] [17592186659746 "![](images/3c/3c45364ee569d9ee24bbac167ad2a76f8a0a1a519f6604b7f9427d723c59abab.png)\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables with the joint probability density function \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6y{e}^{-3x}, & (x,y)\\in D, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $F(x,y)$ is the joint CDF of $X$ and $Y,$ find $F(1,\\frac{1}{3}).$"] [17592186660310 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3(1-x)^{2}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=(1-X)^{3},$ use the change-of-variables method to find the probability density function of $Y.$"] [17592186660344 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2},\\, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=\\frac{1}{3}X+1,$ use the change-of-variables method to find the probability density function of $Y.$"] [17592186660347 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡X,$ use the change-of-variables method to find the probability density function of $Y.$"] [17592186660356 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4\\sqrt[3]{x}}{3}, & 0<x<1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y={e}^{X},$ use the change-of-variables method to find the probability density function of $Y.$"] [17592186660358 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2x}{3}, & 1<x<2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y={log}_{2}⁡X,$ use the change-of-variables method to find the probability density function of $Y.$"] [17592186660371 "Let $X$ be a continuous random variable with the following probability density function:\n\n$$\n{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}},\\, & x>1 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf $Y=X-1,$ use the change-of-variables method to find the probability density function of $Y.$"] [17592186660872 "$$\n{f}_{Y\\,|\\,X}(y\\,|\\,2)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3{y}^{2}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[Y\\,|\\,X=2]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)$ is shown above."] [17592186660880 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}6x, & \\,0\\le x\\le 2-y,\\,1<y<2 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}3(2-y)^{2}, & 1<y<2 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the expression for the conditional expected value $\\text{E}[X\\,|\\,Y=y]$ for $1<y<2.$"] [17592186661486 "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3\\sqrt[3]{y}}, & \\,0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=0]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,0)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|0}=\\frac{2}{5}.$"] [17592186661489 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}, & 0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,0\\le y\\le x, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{7}x\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}, & 0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{3}, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{1}{2}.$"] [17592186661491 "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3{y}^{4/3}}, & \\,1\\le y\\le 8 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=3.$"] [17592186661503 "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{{x}^{6}}, & \\,x\\le -1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=0]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,0)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|0}=-\\frac{5}{4}.$"] [17592186661504 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(x+1)}{3y\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}, & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le 2, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2(x+1)}{3}, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $X$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=\\frac{1}{2}]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|\\frac{1}{2}}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.$"] [17592186661512 "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,-5)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{4}{{y}^{5}}, & \\,y\\le -1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=-5]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,-5)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|-5}=-\\frac{4}{3}.$"] [17592186661515 "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2{x}^{7/2}}, & \\,x\\ge 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|1}=\\frac{5}{3}.$"] [17592186661525 "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{8}, & y=2 \\\\ \\frac{1}{8}, & y=4 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=2]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,2)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|2}=\\frac{9}{4}.$"] [17592186661526 "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,-2)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{3{y}^{10/3}}, & \\,1\\le y \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=-2]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,-2)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|-2}=\\frac{7}{4}.$"] [17592186661535 "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3}\\sqrt[3]{x}, & \\,0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|4}=\\frac{4}{7}.$"] [17592186661541 "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0.8, & y=5 \\\\ 0.2, & y=10 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=4]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,4)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|4}=6.$"] [17592186661543 "$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{{y}^{8}}, & \\,1\\le y \\\\ 0, & \\,\\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$ be continuous random variables. \nFind the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability density function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown above and the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=\\frac{7}{6}.$"] [17592186661544 "$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2+y-x}{2} & 0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,{f}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2y+3}{4}, & 0\\le y\\le 1, \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $X$ and $Y$  be continuous random variables. Their joint probability density function and the marginal probability density function of $Y$ are shown above. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=\\frac{1}{2}]$ given that the corresponding expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|\\frac{1}{2}}=\\frac{11}{24}.$"] [17592186661551 "The joint CDF of two continuous random variables $X$ and $Y$ is given by\n\n$$\nF(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1\\,\\text{or}\\,y<-1 \\\\ \\frac{({x}^{2}-1)({y}^{3}+1)}{2{x}^{2}}, & x\\ge 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ {F}_{X}(x), & x\\ge 1,\\,y>1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the joint PDF $f(x,y)$ for $x\\ge 1,\\,-1\\le y\\le 1.$"] [17592186661553 "The marginal CDFs of two continuous independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}1-{e}^{-4x}, & x\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{1+{y}^{2}}, & y\\ge 0 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the joint CDF when $x\\ge 0$ and $y\\ge 0.$"] [17592186661567 "The marginal CDFs of two continuous independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below. \n\n$$\n{F}_{X}(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}x(x+2), & 0\\le x\\le 1 \\\\ 1, & x>1\\end{aligned}\\,\\,{F}_{Y}(y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & y<0 \\\\ {y}^{5}, & 0\\le y\\le 1 \\\\ 1, & y>1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFind the expression for the joint CDF when $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$"] [17592186662269 "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\bbox[3pt,white,border:2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=0=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?"] [17592186662306 "$$\nA\\text{ is invertible}\\,⇔\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Col}(A)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Col}(A))=n=\\text{rank}(A) \\\\  & \\text{Null}(A)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\text{dim(Null}(A))=\\bbox[3pt,white,border:2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{W}}=\\text{nullity}(A)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $A$ is an $n\\,\\times \\,n$ matrix. Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?"] [17592186665399 "$T$ is a bijection $$\n\\displaystyle \\,⟺\\,\\{\\,\\begin{aligned} & \\text{Im}(T)={R}^{n} \\\\  & \\text{rank}(T)=n \\\\  & \\text{Ker}(T)=\\{0\\} \\\\  & \\bbox[3pt,white,border:2px solid Gainsboro]{\\phantom{WW}}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$ \n$\\,⟺\\,$  $T$ is invertible\n\nConsider the equivalence above, where $T:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{n}$ is a linear transformation whose standard matrix is $T.$ Which of the following should be placed into the blank space to make a true statement?"] [17592186666135 "Given that the sequence ${a}_{n}$ is defined by\n\n$$\n{a}_{n}=\\{\\begin{aligned}2,\\,1\\le n\\le 10 \\\\ 0,\\,n\\ge 11,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ndoes $$\n\\displaystyle {\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }{a}_{n}\n$$ converge or diverge? If it converges, what is the sum of the series?"] [17592186667701 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-4, & x\\ne 2 \\\\ 2, & x=2\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\nI. It is differentiable at $x=1$\n\nII. It is differentiable at $x=2$\n\nIII. It is differentiable on the interval $(-2,2)$"] [17592186670020 "Which of the diagrams shows the solution of the following system?\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}y>-2 \\\\ y\\le -x\\end{aligned}\n$$"]}
